{
  "Source": "access_point_region_evidence.json.gz",
  "Normalization": [
    "Native account 000000000000 maps to 123456789012; native owner IAM user Delegated is represented by local caller/root. This captures endpoint/signature admission, not broader IAM permissions.",
    "Bucket and AP names are deterministic fixture names; alias is bound from the actual CreateAccessPoint response. All source sequences index Observations one-based.",
    "Raw requests preserve Host independently of signing Region and bypass SDK region redirects. Presigned replay expiry is 120 seconds versus captured 60 seconds; both remain unexpired.",
    "Successful list bodies project the backing bucket Name; unrelated default fields and successful regional response headers are not projected. Error XML Region/Endpoint/Bucket and regional response headers retain measured distinctions.",
    "Reopen verifies local retained-backend admission and does not represent an additional native AWS observation.",
    "The copy-source scenario references CopyRegionCapture. It uses fresh west/east buckets and a west AP in the same guarded native account. The failed CLI streaming-body setup attempt is separately preserved as CopyRegionFailedSetup with verified cleanup and is not replayed as an AWS error.",
    "Native copy-source headers are normalized to decoded ARN/alias inputs supported by the existing raw replay; the native HTTP codes, Region details and consumer bytes are retained.",
    "DestinationRegionCapture independently measures direct east bucket source to west AP destination: both ARN/alias CopyObject and UploadPartCopy succeed, unlike cross-region AP sources. Direct-bucket cross-region controls also succeed."
  ],
